# Midterm Project – Recipe Website

## Project Overview

This project is a recipe website focused on Chinese food and 
Chinese–Western fusion comfort meals. The goal of the site is 
to create a warm and welcoming space for Chinese people living 
abroad who may miss the feeling of home.

Food is often strongly connected to memory and emotion. Many 
Chinese students or workers living overseas do not always have 
easy access to home-style meals, so this website collects simple 
recipes that are approachable and comforting. The design of the 
site aims to feel warm, friendly, and home-like rather than overly 
formal.

The website currently includes several recipe pages, images of the 
dishes, ingredients lists, and step-by-step cooking instructions.

---

## Demo of the Site

During the demo I will show the main pages of the website, including 
the homepage and several recipe pages. The navigation bar allows users 
to move between the Home, Recipe, and About sections of the site.

Each recipe page includes:

* Images of the dish
* Ingredients
* Cooking instructions
* A clean layout that is easy to read

I will also demonstrate how the layout responds when the browser window is 
resized. When the screen becomes smaller, the layout adjusts so that images 
and text stack vertically. This makes the site easier to read on phones.

